{"state": {"passage": "Penguins are popularly loved around the world, primarily for their unusually upright, waddling gait, impressive swimming ability and (compared to other birds) lack of fear of humans. Their striking black-and-white plumage is often likened to a white tie suit. Mistakenly, some artists and writers have penguins based at the North Pole. This is incorrect, as there are no wild penguins in the Northern Hemisphere. The cartoon series Chilly Willy helped perpetuate this myth, as the title penguin would interact with northern-hemisphere species, such as polar bears and walruses.", "question": "do any penguins live in the northern hemisphere"}, "questions": {"answer": {"type": "noul", "instructions": "Based on `passage`, is the answer to `question` yes?"}}, "expected": {"answer": false}, "tags": ["boolq", "id:2305", "t3arm:calib"], "language": "en"}
